---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AnswerFacts from '../components/AnswerFacts.astro';
import HelpNow from '../components/HelpNow.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
const all = loadDir('resources');
const office = all.find((e) => e.slug === 'monongalia-county-dohs-office');
const navigator = all.find((e) => e.slug === 'mpls-digital-navigator');
// Stolen SNAP benefits (#1764), from DoHS's own pages, read 2026-11-14.
const stolenSources = [
  { url: 'https://bfa.wv.gov/article/dohs-announces-end-snap-stolen-benefits-replacement', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WV DoHS, January 1, 2025' },
  { url: 'https://bfa.wv.gov/article/dohs-urges-ebt-cardholders-take-steps-now-protect-benefits-skimming', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WV DoHS, April 17, 2025' },
  { url: 'https://bfa.wv.gov/office-ebt', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WV DoHS Office of EBT' },
  { url: 'https://www.fns.usda.gov/snap/stolen-benefits', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'USDA Food and Nutrition Service' },
];
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
export const page = { door: "this-month", topic: "food", label: "Apply for SNAP (food stamps)", summary: "Apply online at WV PATH, or call DoHS" };
---
<Base help title="How to apply for SNAP (food stamps) in Monongalia County, WV" description="Apply for SNAP food help online at WV PATH, the state's free site, or call DoHS customer service. Steps, phone number and sources for Morgantown and Mon County.">
  <h1>How do I apply for SNAP (food stamps) in Mon County?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Apply online at WV PATH, the state's own site. It is free. The steps are below, with the number to call the state Department of Human Services (DoHS) if you have questions.</p>

  <AnswerFacts slug="apply-for-snap-wv-path" linkLabel="Apply at WV PATH" />

  <h2>Work rules for some adults</h2>
  <p>Since November 1, 2025, some adults ages 18 through 64 must meet SNAP work rules to keep getting SNAP. Caring for a child under 14 is one of the reasons a person may not have to. DoHS decides who must meet the rules. For questions, call DoHS at <a href="tel:18777161212">1-877-716-1212</a>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The time limit.</strong> Adults who must meet the rules can get SNAP for "any three (3) months in a 36-month period" unless they meet them. The current period runs from January 1, 2025, to December 31, 2027.</li>
    <li><strong>How to meet them.</strong> Work, or take part in a work program, 80 or more hours a month. "Work does not have to be paid," and volunteering counts.</li>
    <li><strong>Changed in 2025.</strong> DoHS says the old exemptions for "veterans, individuals experiencing homelessness, and former foster youth under age 25" were removed. People in these groups now meet the rules unless another exemption fits.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="meta">Sources: <a href="https://dohs.wv.gov/article/west-virginia-announces-changes-snap-able-bodied-adults-without-dependents-abawd-policy">West Virginia DoHS</a>, checked November 2, 2026; <a href="https://bfa.wv.gov/media/1761/download?inline">DoHS SNAP work requirement fact sheet (PDF)</a>, checked November 2, 2026.</p>

  <h2 id="help-with-the-form">Want someone to help you with the online form?</h2>
  <p>The library's Digital Navigator holds drop-in hours where you can ask about "online forms and applications," email and online accounts. It is a walk-in, with no appointment. For SNAP rules and questions about your case, DoHS answers at <a href="tel:18777161212">1-877-716-1212</a>.</p>
  {navigator && <ResourceCard r={navigator} />}

  <h2>Rather apply in person?</h2>
  {office && <ResourceCard r={office} />}

  <h2 id="stolen">If your SNAP benefits were stolen</h2>
  <p>Thieves can copy an EBT card with a "skimmer" hidden on a card reader, then spend the benefits, often in another state. If you think your card or benefits were stolen:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Call the number on the back of your EBT card, <a href="tel:18665456502">1-866-545-6502</a>. It is open 24 hours a day. You can report a lost or stolen card and get help changing your PIN.</li>
    <li>Change your PIN right away. The USDA says this stops the thief from making new purchases.</li>
    <li>Tell DoHS. Call the Office of EBT at <a href="tel:3045584126">304-558-4126</a> or DoHS customer service at <a href="tel:18777161212">1-877-716-1212</a>, or go to the county DoHS office above.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Can you get them back?</strong> DoHS says its power to replace stolen SNAP benefits ended on December 20, 2024, and claims for benefits stolen after that date "will be denied." If your benefits were stolen between October 1, 2022, and December 20, 2024, you may still file a claim at the county DoHS office or at <a href="tel:18777161212">1-877-716-1212</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>To protect your card,</strong> DoHS suggests:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Check the card reader for loose parts, tape or wires before you use it.</li>
    <li>Change your PIN each month, before your benefits come.</li>
    <li>Block out-of-state purchases at ebtEDGE.com or in the ebtEDGE app. You can turn the block off when you need to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The USDA says state agencies and EBT companies will never call or text to ask for your PIN or card number.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={stolenSources} about="stolen SNAP benefits" />

  <p>SNAP can also buy seeds and plants that grow food. See <a href={`${base}/grow/#budget`}>Grow food on a budget</a>.</p>

  <p>Already applied? See <a href={`${base}/after-you-apply/snap/`}>what happens after you apply for SNAP</a>: the interview, letters, deadlines and how to appeal.</p>

  <HelpNow />

  <p class="meta">We describe how to apply. The state decides who gets SNAP. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
